From: ultimatejeeves <ultimatejeeves@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:47:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 12/43] JS: sound through a ring in the heap for the page's
 AudioWorklet

The OpenAL path queued ~100 ms buffers through the page's main thread and started playing with one
buffer queued, so each next buffer arrived just as the last ran out: any main-thread or emulation
jitter was an audible gap. CSH_WsxRing writes ~11 ms pieces (11 SPU blocks) into a ring the page's
AudioWorklet reads from the audio thread (getAudioRingAddress). Volume moved to the page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
